label ch03:

    # c03.s01
    scene cg c3_needle_ride
    with fade
    "The needle did not move through the water so much as decline to be where it had been."

    "Wrack clung to Okonta's back with his eyes shut for the first hour. There was no sense of an engine. There was no noise at all but a thin high singing from the hull, and the pressure of the sea against his shoulders."
    "When he opened his eyes the forest was going past in a gold blur, and she was steering with nothing. There was no wheel and no lever. There was only a slight leaning of her shoulders, as a swimmer leans."

    scene bg kelp_forest
    with dissolve
    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_wrack "You feel it,"
    c_wrack "Like a limb."
    c_okonta "Like a limb. And I hear through it. The hull listens to the water for me, a long way off."
    "She tapped the scar at her temple."
    show p okonta_wry as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "That's the Thread. It's a thing he puts in, finer than a hair, from here down the back of the neck. After that the old machines know you. There are a hundred or so of us left, and no two of us agree about anything, which is how he likes it."

    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_wrack "Where are we going?"
    c_okonta "Greywatch Stone. The Dragon's due there in six days, if the almanac's right. It's been wrong lately."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    scene cg c3_moored_night
    with dissolve
    "They stopped when the light failed. She moored the needle to a kelp stem with a loop of cord, as one might tie up a horse, and it hung there with its faint light pulsing slowly, like something asleep."
    "She gave him dried fish from a pouch, and a strip of something chewy and sweet that she said was cured sea-pear. Then she lay back in the water with her hands behind her head."

    "The forest was different at night. The chord was still there, but above it now, far off and very high, something else was singing."
    "It was a long falling phrase, and then a pause, and then an answer from another quarter, fainter."

    scene bg kelp_night
    with dissolve
    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_listening as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "Pale singers,"
    c_okonta "Whales. White ones, as big as a hold's dome. They come down from the ice at this season to calve. That one's two hundred kilometres north of us, and the one answering is further."
    "She listened with her eyes closed."
    c_okonta "Every one of them sings its own water. The old pilots learned the songs, and so did I. If I hear that cow, I know where the Greywatch rise is from here without looking. Agravars have instruments for it. I've seen them. Dials."

    c_wrack "You've been on the islands?"
    show p okonta_wry as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "I've been on their ships. Mostly while removing them."
    "She opened one eye."
    c_okonta "You want to know what I am. Ask. You've a week of my back to look at."

    "So he asked, and she told him, in a voice with no decoration in it."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "She had been born in Deep Chorus, the great canyon hold, three days south. She had been a herder's daughter and then a herder. When she was twenty-six an agravar trawler had come over the canyon mouth with its gear down."
    "It was fishing where the charts said nobody lived. It took four hundred silverbacks, and her brother, who had been among them. The elders of Deep Chorus had sung for him and held a council and done nothing, because there was nothing they could do."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "So I went to Greywatch and sat on a bench for two seasons,"
    c_okonta "The Dragon came by twice. The first time there was no one to carry me aboard. The second time there was a Threaded with a spare seat. I rode to the top of the world and told a little old man in an apron that I wanted to be made into a weapon."
    "She smiled slightly at the dark."
    show p okonta_wry as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "He said he didn't make those any more. He said he could make me into a pair of ears and a fast horse, and that if I still wanted it after a year of gutting fish for the Lantern, I could have it. I gutted fish for fourteen months."

    c_wrack "And then?"

    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "And then there's a rule. It isn't long."
    c_okonta "{i}Keep the water. Own nothing you can't carry. Come when you're called.{/i} You say it to him once and he never mentions it again."
    "She shifted."
    c_okonta "I keep the water between Rime and the Slick. I turn their survey boats round. I cut their trawl lines, and I pull people out of wrecks, theirs as well as ours. I've sunk eleven hulls in thirty years and not one with a crew aboard. He minds about that. It used to make me angry."
    "She was quiet for a time."
    show p okonta_sorrow as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "I wasn't near enough to Low Anthem. One of me, and a stretch of sea you couldn't swim across in a month. There were three of us on this water when I started."

    show p wrack_tunic_troubled as left at head_left
    with qd
    c_wrack "What is he like?"
    show p okonta_wry as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "He'll disappoint you,"
    c_okonta "Everybody's disappointed, the first day. Go to sleep."

    # c03.s02
    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    scene bg kelp_forest
    with fade
    "On the second day she stiffened and brought the needle to a dead halt."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_listening as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "Engines,"
    c_okonta "Four. Behind us, coming on a line."
    "She listened a moment longer, with her head tilted, to something he could not hear."
    c_okonta "Sleds. Halcyon make. That barge crew talked, and somebody ashore has decided they'd like whatever picked up their ship. That's a recovery team. They'll have wreckers with them, to find the way."

    c_wrack "Wreckers?"
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "Divers. Islanders, the kind with no corporation. They go down on drowned Maker ruins and tear out anything that shines, and they sell it to the shipyards. They know the bottom better than the companies do."
    "She spat a little stream of water sideways."
    c_okonta "Vermin, mostly. Good at their work."

    c_wrack "Can we outrun them?"
    show p okonta_urgent as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "I can outrun anything they've got. I can't outrun a bounty. Every wrecker between here and the Girdle will have your description by tomorrow."
    "She turned the needle south-east."
    c_okonta "We'll go where they won't want to follow."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    scene bg tangle
    with dissolve
    "The Tangle was the forest gone wild. Nobody farmed it and nobody thinned it. The kelp grew so thick that the stems rubbed together and groaned, and the light failed a few metres in."
    "Okonta slowed to a crawl and the needle's glow went ahead of them like a held lamp. Old wrecks loomed out of the murk."
    "They were agravar hulls from wars two hundred years gone, lying on their sides, furred with weed, with fish going in and out of the gun-ports. Once the needle's light fell on a skull in a rusted helmet, and something with many legs looked out of the eye."

    "Twice Wrack saw lights moving far off between the stems, yellow-green, and felt himself watched."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "Breakers,"
    c_okonta "They'll leave us alone. They don't quarrel with the Thread."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "He wondered if Hesper was among them. He thought of her face at the kelp stem. He did not think she would be carrying a light."

    scene bg sounding_ruin
    with dissolve
    "On the third day the ground under them began to rise, and the kelp thinned, and they came out over something he took at first for a hill."

    "It was a dome. It was three times the size of Low Anthem's, and it had been broken open like an egg. Half of it stood. Even the wild kelp had left a ring of bare sand around the place, as around a grave."

    "The needle had slowed without his noticing. Okonta was looking down."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_sorrow as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "That was a hold called Sounding,"
    c_okonta "Six thousand people. It's been like that nine hundred years."
    "She put her hand flat on the hull and the needle moved on."
    c_okonta "The last time mariners went to war with each other, that's what it looked like. There were eleven of those when it was over. It's why we've no army, and no king, and no hold that tells another what to do. We frightened ourselves."
    "She glanced back at him over her shoulder."
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "He was born there. Jef. Don't bring it up unless he does."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "The engines followed them in. They were clumsy in the kelp, but there were four of them and they had lamps and patience. By that evening Okonta's mouth had set in a line."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_urgent as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "They're herding us,"
    c_okonta "Someone on that team knows this ground. There's only one way out that they haven't covered."

    c_wrack "Which way?"

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "She did not answer. An hour later he knew."

    scene bg slick_edge
    with dissolve
    "The kelp ended. It did not thin; it stopped, at a line as sharp as a shoreline, and beyond it there was nothing. There were no fish. There was no hum."
    "He had lived inside that chord for three weeks and had stopped hearing it, and its absence now was like a hand over his ears."
    "In front of them, in neat rows, stood the bitterwrack that some hold's old women had planted years ago, a wall of it a hundred metres deep. Every plant was black to the root, and dead. The water beyond was the colour of strong tea. Things hung in it, in shreds, that did not sink or rise."

    show p wrack_tunic_frightened as left at head_left
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "The Slick,"
    c_okonta "Twenty years of barges, settled in one place by the current. The carrying crews bring the bladders here too; there's nowhere else to take them. Keep your mouth shut as much as you can. We go straight through."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "They were a kilometre in when the needle shuddered. Something had hold of the tail."

    scene cg c3_eel
    with dissolve
    "Wrack looked back and saw it. It was an eel as thick as his body and as long as the needle. A second came up out of the silt beneath them. A third."
    c_okonta "Slick eels,"
    c_okonta "They hunt by taste. Hold on."
    "She threw the needle sideways. The first eel lost its grip, and the second struck the hull so hard that Wrack's hands tore free."
    "He was in the water, spinning. The taste of it was in his mouth, oily and sweet. An eel turned towards him with its jaws opening like a split hose."

    scene bg slick_edge
    with dissolve
    "He reached for the sea. {i}Please{/i}, he thought, as Hesper had taught him. {i}Please.{/i}"

    "Nothing."

    "It was not like being ebbed. When he was ebbed, a door had been shut, and he had known there was a house behind it."
    "Here there was no door and no house. He was asking a dead thing to speak. The water around him was only water, heavy and filthy, and he was a man in a borrowed tunic with nothing in his hands."

    "The eel came on. Then the needle went through it. Okonta had turned in her own length, impossibly."
    "She took the thing behind the head with the needle's prow and carried it thirty metres. She came round again and hooked an arm through Wrack's as she passed."

    show p wrack_tunic_shaken as left at head_left
    show p okonta_urgent as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "Deaf water!"
    "she shouted."
    c_okonta "The gift doesn't answer here. Did nobody tell you?"

    c_wrack "Nobody told me anything!"

    c_okonta "Then you've learned it cheap. Remember it. There's water that's fouled, where she hears you badly. And there's water like this, where she isn't. Where they've killed her."
    "The needle was running flat out and the dead brown fog streamed past them."
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "It's the one thing the Breakers are right about. She can die. A bit at a time."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    scene bg kelp_forest
    with dissolve
    "They came out the far side an hour later into clean sea. He hung onto her back and coughed black threads into the current. He found that he was weeping, though not for himself."
    "He had not known the sea could be killed. And a thought had come to him in the middle of that silence, and would not go away. He had not been surprised. Somewhere under the blank, he had known that place was there."

    # c03.s03
    scene bg greywatch_stone
    with fade
    "Greywatch Stone stood on a bare rise above the forest, where the kelp would not grow and the current ran strong and cold."

    "Every surface of the benches had been scratched with names. So had the paving, and the pillar's foot as high as a hand could reach."
    "The names were in the mariners' looping script, thousands of them, some sharp and new, most worn nearly smooth. Many had a tally of strokes beside them, to show how many days the writer had waited."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "It's a calling stone,"
    c_okonta "There are forty or so, strung round the world along the lines the Dragon runs. It passes each of them once a season, more or less. The world turns under it, you see; it never runs the same line twice running."
    "She took a little book of sea-silk leaves from her suit and turned it, frowning."
    c_okonta "That's what the almanacs are for. Every hold keeps one, and it's handed down. This was my teacher's. It says the sixth day from when we started, at the turn of the morning watch."

    c_wrack "And the stone?"

    c_okonta "When the Dragon's within a day, it sings. You'll know."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "They were not alone on the rise. A woman of about thirty sat there with an old man who lay propped against a bundle, breathing as though each breath had to be lifted. They were from Fallow, the hold next to Low Anthem."
    "She had towed her father here on a sled of kelp-floats, eleven days, because the healer at Fallow had said his lungs needed the Wells, and nothing less. They had been at the stone since before the last pass."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p fallow_woman_weary as right at head_right
    with qd
    "It came, and there was no Threaded to carry us on,"
    "She had a tired, flat, capable way of speaking."
    "So we stayed. He won't last another season. I thought, if one of you came by this time."
    show p fallow_woman_hopeful as right at head_right
    with qd
    "She looked at the needle, and then, hopefully, at Okonta."

    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with dissolve
    c_okonta "I've a passenger,"
    c_okonta "I'll come back for you when he's aboard. It's in the rule."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "There was a third traveller. He was sitting on a bale as big as himself, and he had not stopped watching Wrack since they arrived. His name was Brask. He was an ice-diver of Rime, the one hold at the top of the world, going home with a season's trade of kelp-cake and rope."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p brask_watchful as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_brask "You're the lamp man,"
    "He had a voice like a slab of something being dropped."
    c_brask "It's all down the long-call. A stranger's hands."
    "He looked Wrack over, slowly, from the feet up."
    show p brask_gruff as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_brask "You're not much."

    show p wrack_tunic_calm as left at head_left
    with qd
    c_wrack "No,"
    "Wrack agreed."

    c_brask "Jef's not much either."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "Brask seemed to think this settled something. He reached into the bale and produced a slab of smoked fish the size of a roof slate, broke it in four, and handed it round."

    "They waited. The fourth day went by, and the fifth. Wrack read the names on the benches. He sat with the old man from Fallow while the daughter slept."
    "The old man had no breath for talk, but he liked to have the names read to him, and now and then he would lift a finger at one he had known. The stone stayed silent. The almanac said the sixth day."

    scene cg c3_sleds
    with dissolve
    "On the sixth day it was the engines that came."

    "Four grey sleds came up over the rise in a line. They were squat ugly machines with caged screws, and armoured divers rode them with harpoon guns levelled. The woman from Fallow threw herself across her father. Brask stood up off his bale with a seal-spear in his fist. Okonta moved in front of Wrack."

    scene bg greywatch_stone
    with dissolve
    show p wrack_tunic_troubled as left at head_left
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "There's nowhere to go,"
    "she said quietly."
    c_okonta "I could carry you off. But the Dragon will pass, and those two will be left here with that lot. And there won't be another pass for a season."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "The lead diver dismounted. She was an officer, by the stripe on her helmet. She raised her faceplate lamp and the beam found Wrack's face."

    "She stopped."

    "Even through the helmet glass he could see her go white. Her gun dropped a hand's width. Her mouth moved, and the suit speaker carried it clearly across the water."

    show p wrack_tunic_baffled as left at head_left
    show p officer_shocked as right at head_right
    with qd
    "{i}Sir?{/i}"

    "Nobody moved."

    show p officer_hard as right at head_right
    with qd
    "Then her face closed. She brought the gun up again."
    "Take him,"
    "Alive. He wants him breathing. That's the order. Leave the others."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "It was then that the stone began to sing."

    "It was one note, so low that the sand on the paving danced to it. A moment later the sea answered from the north, on the same note. It was felt in the chest before it was heard. The divers turned. The benches trembled."

    scene cg c3_dragon_arrives
    with dissolve
    "Far off in the dark something pale appeared. It was a thread, then a rope, then a river, and Wrack forgot the guns."

    "He had imagined an animal. What came was a river with a spine. A kilometre of pale metal ribs, each one a hoop taller than the dome of Low Anthem, ran one behind another in a long sinuous line, and between them and through them and around them raced water."
    "It was not the water of the sea. It was bound to the ribs, a brighter, denser stuff, shining faintly from inside, and it poured forward along the frame without ever leaving it, as a flame streams back from a torch."
    "That was what gave the thing its body. That was what made it move. It came on faster than anything that size had a right to, and it sang as it came, and the whole forest below it leaned over in its wake."

    scene bg greywatch_stone
    with dissolve
    "It never stopped. Okonta had told him so. You matched its speed, and showed your token, and it opened to you or it did not."

    "It was past the first sled before the divers could scatter."

    "And then it slowed."

    "It slowed, and the note fell and fell. For the first time in the memory of anyone living, the Dragon stopped. It hung in the water above Greywatch Stone with its whole length humming."

    scene cg c3_dragon_head
    with dissolve
    "The great blunt head swung round, over the heads of the Halcyon divers, until it was facing Wrack. It had no eyes and no mouth. A panel in it, which he had somehow known was there, slid open like an eyelid."

    c_okonta "It has never done that,"
    "Okonta said, very quietly."
    c_okonta "Not for me. Not for anyone. Not for Jef."

    "The divers had backed off to the edge of the rise. Not one of them had a gun up."

    "Wrack swam forward and laid his palm on the metal. It was warm. And under his hand he could feel what was wrong with it, the way you feel a splinter. There were a hundred small failures. Bearings were worn and channels silted, and at the centre a great heart was labouring."

    scene bg greywatch_stone
    with dissolve
    show p wrack_tunic_soft as left at head_left
    with qd
    c_wrack "It's tired,"
    c_wrack "It's so tired."

    hide left
    with qd
    "He did not think about what he did next. He asked the sea, gently this time, and the bound water in the Dragon's ribs moved for him. It flushed the silted channels one by one."
    "His hands went into the open panel and found the worst of it. Then both things were happening at once. The water worked where his fingers could not reach, and his fingers worked where water was no use, and for a little while he was not afraid of anything."

    "The note rose again. It was clearer than before."

    show p wrack_tunic_awed as left at head_left
    show p okonta_urgent as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "Get in,"
    "She was staring at him."
    c_okonta "All of you. You, with your father. You, with the beard, bring your wretched bale. Get in before they remember what they're paid for."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "He looked back once from the panel. The officer was still standing where she had stopped, with her lamp on him and her gun hanging at her side."

    "Then the Dragon closed its eye and ran north."

    # c03.s04
    scene bg gallery
    with fade
    "He had expected the inside of a machine. It was more like the inside of a song."

    "The panel had let them into a single hall that ran the whole length of the Dragon. The mariners called it the gallery. It was flooded, and warm, and the water in it was perfectly still, though the thing was moving faster than the needle ever had."
    "There was only the bound water, pouring past, bright and clear as glass. He was looking out through it as through the back of a waterfall, and the whole sea was going by."

    "For three thousand years people had made themselves at home there. There were names scratched here too, in a band along the floor, a kilometre of names. Low in the belly was a row of cradles shaped to the needles, and Okonta laid hers into one, where it settled with a click."

    scene bg cradles
    with dissolve
    "Each cradle had a name cut beside it. One near the end stood empty, with silt in it. The name beside that one was short and square, and it was not a mariner's name. Somebody had once tried to scratch it out, and had given up."

    scene bg gallery
    with dissolve
    "And the walls hummed. The note was everywhere. After an hour he ceased to hear it, and after a day he could not imagine silence."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p okonta_grave as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_okonta "Nobody knows what it was for,"
    "She had hung a hammock with the ease of long habit."
    c_okonta "A road, I think. The Makers had cities all round the world and this went between them. Now it's all the road there is. There's no other way from one end of Ovara to the other that doesn't take half a year and likely kill you."
    "She looked up the long shining hall."
    c_okonta "I've ridden it forty times. I've never once seen it empty of somebody going to the Wells to be mended. That's what it's really become. An ambulance."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "The woman from Fallow had settled her father in a net near the wall, where he could see out. His breathing had eased a little in the warmth. She came to Wrack that first evening, twisting her hands, and tried to thank him. He did not know what to do with it."

    show p wrack_tunic_troubled as left at head_left
    show p fallow_woman_relieved as right at head_right
    with qd
    "It stopped for him,"
    "she said to Okonta afterwards, not quite out of his hearing."
    "It {i}stopped{/i}. What is he?"

    show p okonta_wry as right at head_right
    with dissolve
    c_okonta "A man who can't work a gate latch,"
    c_okonta "Leave him be."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "They ran north for three days, and he watched the world go by."

    "On the first day it was the forest, seen from above, an endless gold canopy rippling in their wake. The lit domes of holds stood up through it like lamps in a field. He counted nine."
    "Twice there was a hold that showed only the faint green-yellow of lampweed, and once a dome that showed nothing at all. Nobody in the gallery spoke as they passed over it."

    "That night the pale singers found them. He woke to the song, close, and went to the wall."

    scene cg c3_whales
    with dissolve
    "There were six of them, running alongside. They kept pace for an hour without visible effort, rolling to look in through the bound water at the people inside."
    "Their voices came through the wall and through his ribs. A calf no bigger than a fishing boat swam so near that he could see the scars on its mother's flank."

    scene bg gallery
    with dissolve
    show p wrack_tunic_awed as left at head_left
    show p brask_awed as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_brask "They like it,"
    "Brask said, beside him. The big man had come to watch with his arms folded."
    c_brask "My grandmother says they think it's one of them. A slow old cow that's lost her voice and only knows the one note."
    "He grunted."
    show p brask_gruff as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_brask "They'll leave it at the ice. They don't care for the ice."

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "On the second day the forest ended and the water darkened to a deep cold blue. The bottom fell away. Now there was nothing to see below them but distance, and above them the surface, like a ceiling of beaten silver."
    "The cold came through even the bound water, and Brask at last looked comfortable. Wrack spent that day with his hands inside the Dragon's workings. He had found that the floor of the gallery opened, here and there, on seams like the lamp's."
    "He lay on his stomach for hours with his arms in to the shoulder, clearing channels, seating things that had slipped. He did not understand what he was doing. He understood it as you understand how to catch something thrown at you."

    show p wrack_tunic_attentive as left at head_left
    show p brask_watchful as right at head_right
    with qd
    "Brask watched this too, and at length sat down beside him with a companionable thud."

    c_brask "You'll want to know about the Pale,"
